Package: rpi-headtracker
Architecture: arm64
Depends: adduser, kmod, ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: head tracker for sim racing that works as a USB joystick
 Turns a Raspberry Pi with a camera into a head tracker: the camera follows
 the driver's head and the Pi sends the head's turn and tilt to the PC as a
 USB joystick. Sims bind it like any game controller; no driver or software
 is needed on the PC.
 .
 Settings, a live view and help are on a web page (port 18080). Two face
 models: YuNet (OpenCV) and NeuralNet (the opentrack NeuralNet models, run
 with a private copy of ONNX Runtime).
 .
 Needs a Pi whose USB-C port can work as a device (Pi 4, Pi 5, Zero 2 W,
 CM4) and a 64-bit Raspberry Pi OS. The package turns on device mode for that
 port in config.txt; it takes effect after a restart.
